        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Microcontroller sheet, page 2/4: U1 pin 8 is labeled EN/CHIP_PU; C14 is labeled 1uF between +3V3 and the EN node, and C7 is labeled 10uF from that node to GND."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EN pin lacks a defined DC pull-up, so the ESP32-C3 may fail to start or reset unpredictably; any internal weak bias may not provide the intended reliable reset behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The EN/CHIP_PU circuitry appears to AC-couple +3V3 through C14 rather than provide a DC pull-up, while C7 pulls the EN node toward GND. This can prevent reliable startup or reset of the controller."
}

